<h2>Public Comments</h2>
<p>(The following public comments are available in Japanese)</p>
<table class="no-border" style="width: 100%;">
 <tbody>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 9, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/news/30/ginkou/kouhilyoubunn_20180309.html">Publication of the draft amendments to the “Order for Enforcement of the Banking Act”</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The FSA proposed the draft amendments to the “Order for Enforcement of the Banking Act,” pertaining to the enforcement of the “Act for Partial Revision of the Banking Act (Act No. 49 of 2017),” which mainly aims to introduce a registration system for electronic payment service providers.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 7, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/news/30/ginkou/20180307.html">Publication of the finalized amendments to the regulatory notice on the liquidity coverage ratio</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The FSA finalized the amendments to the regulatory notice on the liquidity coverage ratio for internationally active banks. The amendments reflect the updates from the “Basel III – The Liquidity Coverage Ratio framework: frequently asked questions (as of January 2013)” which was published in June 2017.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 5, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/news/29/sonota/20180226.html">Publication of the draft amendments to the cabinet office order to amend the “Rules on Registration of Certified Public Accountants”</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The FSA proposed the draft amendments to the cabinet office order to amend the “Rules on Registration of Certified Public Accountants.” To mitigate the burden of an applicant in filing an application for registration as a certified public accountant, the proposal mainly aims to clarify that an applicant is not required to submit a transcript of the family register unless he/she is subject to certain conditions.</td>
  </tr>
 </tbody>
</table>
