<p><br><span style="font-weight: bold;"><span class="kakomi-b">Others</span></span></p>
<table class="no-border" style="width: 100%;">
 <tbody>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 8, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/ordinary/chuui/index.html">Warnings about entities that are operating money lending businesses without proper registration</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The FSA (Local Finance Bureaus) updated warnings about entities that are operating money lending businesses without proper registration. The warnings include the updated list of entities that misrepresent their registration using fictitious or stolen registration numbers.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 8, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/news/30/virtual_currency/20180308-1.html">Administrative action against Coincheck inc. (The Kanto Local Finance Bureau)</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The Kanto Local Finance Bureau took an administrative action against Coincheck inc., ordering the improvement of its business operations pursuant to the “Payment Services Act.” This administrative action is based on the findings from the FSA’s on-site inspection in which the said entity was found to have serious issues pertaining to its business management structure and internal control system.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 8, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/news/30/virtual_currency/20180308-7.html">Administrative action against Tech Bureau, Corp. (The Kinki Local Finance Bureau)</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The Kinki Local Finance Bureau took an administrative action against Tech Bureau, Corp., ordering the improvement of its business operations pursuant to the “Payment Services Act.” This administrative action is based on the findings from the FSA’s on-site inspection in which the said entity was found to have a certain inappropriateness from the customer protection perspective for having failed to establish respective systems to ensure effective system risk management and appropriate customer services.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 8, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/news/30/virtual_currency/20180308-6.html">Administrative action against GMO Coin, Inc. (The Kanto Local Finance Bureau)</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The Kanto Local Finance Bureau took an administrative action against GMO Coin, Inc., ordering the improvement of its business operations pursuant to the “Payment Services Act.” This administrative action is based on the findings from the FSA’s on-site inspection in which the said entity was found to have failed to establish an effective system risk management system.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 8, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/news/30/virtual_currency/20180308-2.html">Administrative action against FSHO Kabushiki Kaisha* (The Kanto Local Finance Bureau)</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The Kanto Local Finance Bureau took an administrative action against FSHO Kabushiki Kaisha*, ordering the suspension of its business from March 8 to April 7, 2018 and the improvement of its business operations pursuant to the “Payment Services Act.” This administrative action is based on the findings from the FSA’s on-site inspection, in which the said entity was found to be in violation of the “Payment Services Act,” mainly in terms of user protection. 
    <p class="in-1 mb-0">* This corporate name is not available in English and is the Romanized version of its Japanese name.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 8, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/news/30/virtual_currency/20180308-3.html">Administrative action against bit station Kabushiki Kaisha* (The Tokai Local Finance Bureau)</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The Tokai Local Finance Bureau took an administrative action against bit station Kabushiki Kaisha*, ordering the suspension of its business from March 8 to April 7, 2018 and the improvement of its business operations pursuant to the “Payment Services Act.” This administrative action is based on the findings from the FSA’s on-site inspection, in which the said entity was found to be in violation of the “Payment Services Act,” mainly in terms of user protection. 
    <p class="in-1 mb-0">* This corporate name is not available in English and is the Romanized version of its Japanese name.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <th class="m-d-y" nowrap style="width: 19%; text-align: left;">March 8, 2018</th>
   <td><a target="_blank" href="/news/30/virtual_currency/20180308-4.html">Administrative action against Bicrements, Inc. (The Kanto Local Finance Bureau)</a><img alt="open new window" class="newwin" style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" src="/en/images/common/icon_newwin.gif"><br><span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&lt; </span>Summary<span lang="EN-US" new="" style="font-family:;" times="">&gt;</span><br>
     The Kanto Local Finance Bureau took an administrative action against Bicrements, Inc., ordering the improvement of its business operations pursuant to the “Payment Services Act.” This administrative action is based on the findings from the FSA’s on-site inspection. The said entity’s business management structure was deemed insufficient in terms of the effectiveness to ensure regulatory compliance and appropriate business operations, in which the entity was found to have failed to conduct internal audits. The entity’s business operational status was also deemed problematic mainly in terms of the segregation management of users’ assets and the preparation and keeping of books and documents.</td>
